        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: beta releases require manual reruns after plugin publication",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where beta publication could require repeated operator reruns when plugin npm failed after ClawHub had already been dispatched, or when ClawHub's asynchronous security promotion outlasted the verifier. It also forward-ports the release-preparation, Signal shutdown, extension-cache, Codex fixture, memory-vault, Telegram diagnostic, and QA metadata fixes proven while producing `2026.7.2-beta.3`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis forward-port was rebased onto current `main` after the beta completed. Plugin npm must now succeed before ClawHub dispatch; ClawHub verification gets a bounded full-queue retry horizon with lower polling concurrency. Accepted Signal ingress drains before monitor disposal, and the release/test harness fixes remove observed flakes without weakening validation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRelease operators keep the same package, registry, and exact-SHA confidence gates with fewer manual retries and no stale ClawHub child occupying the release environment after npm failure. Signal users no longer risk an accepted in-flight message being abandoned during Gateway shutdown.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Published beta: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases/tag/v2026.7.2-beta.3\n- Full Release Validation: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29660853502\n- npm preflight: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29662726100\n- successful parent publish: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29664100317\n- plugin npm retry after authorization repair: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29664738469\n- complete ClawHub verification, 225/225 jobs: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29664739655\n- focused Testbox proof after final rebase: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29667788917 — 409 tests passed across release tooling, Signal, Codex, memory-wiki, and QA taxonomy\n- changed-surface gate after final rebase: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29667795138 — typecheck, lint, formatting, plugin boundaries, SDK manifest, import cycles, and repository guards passed\n- temp-fixture cleanup proof: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29668095243 — 8/8 focused tests passed; warning-only temp-directory guard is clean\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (confidence 0.88)\n\nAI-assisted: Codex.\n",
